{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Also our land.</b> The language of death and vitality applies even to something that is not alive, as it says: ״ואתה מחיה את כולם״. And further, if one does not plow and work it and it does not produce fruit, it is as though dead." "<b>We, and our land, slaves to Pharaoh. We</b> — to serve him; <b>and our land</b> — to give him a tax from it."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:53.096114064Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}